## Mandatory Planning Test

The unchanged declared planning rule gives

$$
160\times 8.534247625=1365.47962\ \mathrm{s}<1800\ \mathrm{s}.
$$

Plainly: the prescribed projection is about 22.8 minutes and fits the unchanged 30-minute allowance. This passes the planning test; it is not an upper or lower bound on the actual full runtime.

Later cells touch different pieces, and whole-attempt preparation, independent checking and publication costs do not scale identically. Simple raw-stream projections are 21,865,440 row bytes and 7,103,040 piece bytes; these are planning estimates, not output-size proofs. The actual full attempt must still stop on any original deadline, memory, output, monitoring or mathematical failure. A failure does not authorize retries, more workers, longer time, smaller history allowances or easier mathematics.

Plainly: favorable extrapolation permits consideration of one bounded full attempt, not a promise that it will finish.

## Exact Full Attempt And Unchanged Stops

The prospective scope is literal `full`: recompute all 160 closed cells from the original 161 exact knots, including cell zero. Require 10,240 pair-cell records, 8,960 ordinary nonself records, 1,280 explicit self exclusions, 17,920 distinct nonself face checks and 17,920 compact piece records. No pilot-prefix reuse, skipped pair, resumed stream or partial-run promotion is allowed. Keep all eight identities, original charges, normalized wake speed `1`, 1,760 pieces per member, retained domain `[-8,0.13]`, 90-digit outward arithmetic, original scalar allowances, speed `0.85`, clearance `0.27`, factor floor `1e-24` and emission proposal `[-8,a-0.05]` for reception cell `[a,b]`.

Plainly: the faster implementation owes the entire original calculation again. It does not get a reduced scientific target.

| Control | Full-attempt requirement |
| --- | --- |
| Concurrency | One serial consumer followed by one independent comparison; zero EOM workers; no concurrent F5 response or other F6c pilot/full attempt |
| Inclusive deadline | 1800 seconds from external launcher start through capture, both stages, final publication, rechecks, cleanup and successfully flushed final completion |
| Memory | Aggregate owned-process RSS samples no more than one second apart; stop at 2 GiB or loss of valid observation |
| Heartbeat | Flushed external stage, elapsed time and observed row progress every 15 seconds |
| Host admission | At least 40 percent free memory and 64 GiB available disk |
| Host stops | Below 20 percent free memory or 16 GiB available disk; observations every 15 seconds and after process closure, with two-second query deadlines |
| File limits | At most 64 MiB for each scientific input, raw subject output and comparison output; original bounded runtime capture preserved |
| Log limit | At most 16 MiB combined operational logs and rejection diagnostics |
| Exclusive attempt | Fresh ignored directory under the existing lane; the unchanged shared `.pilot.lock`; no stale-lock stealing, overwrite, automatic retry or resume |

Plainly: every safety limit stays in place. A faster pilot does not grant a larger resource budget.

Before execution, independently freeze the separate full entrypoint, launcher and controls and the exact machine plan, including the accepted consumer `af53f5af2f9dd7eda4869af2a7533f869f4e3866003c90bf9a8487b2e5636386`, cached library `daa4cc227cb8685de673fc400d817a19666b4fc7323e6c3a56f475a463b23acf` and independent comparison `19c57e9b638b0beb866c86b061b2325f9567add2a85608f0c42ef1f7612d9132`. Bind this plan, the original resource plan, the completed pilot and its runtime/source closure. Execute only captured source generations with the resolved shared-venv interpreter and bound operational executables. The supervisor must reject pilot/full scope mismatches, incomplete census, source drift, changed evidence, lost ownership, late publication and failed cleanup. All original mathematical and operational rejection conditions continue to apply.

Plainly: a new full-run supervisor needs its own review. The approved pilot launcher remains pilot-only and is not modified or reused to bypass its scope restriction.

## Disposition And Excluded Claims

The planning arithmetic passes conditionally on independent acceptance of the named completed pilot and this plan. Actual full execution remains not-run until the separately reviewed operational composition and exact machine plan are accepted. Subsequent acceptance and outcome belong in the mutable launch-readiness owner rather than revisions of this frozen plan. Preserve the old resource return, new raw evidence, failed/not-run dispositions and all false library authority flags.

Plainly: this document is a frozen proposal with measurable prerequisites. A later status update cannot rewrite its inputs or claim that unfinished work ran.

Even a completed full cover establishes only conditional reconstructed-family root coverage. It establishes no historical trajectory identity, new root refinement, acceleration or residual measurement, quadrature, peak, `M05/M06`, H3 promotion, metric, score, ordinary EOM evolution, equilibrium, binding, retention, return, stability or physical realization. Falsifiers are an incorrect bound hash, a mismatch with the original caller-observed completion, failed planning arithmetic, changed scientific scope or limit, missing pair/piece/face, or any lost monitoring, process closure or final-publication obligation.

Plainly: computational readiness is not evidence that a braid sustains itself.

Closure goal: independently accept this measured plan and a separately frozen full operational composition before one fresh full root-cover attempt under the unchanged limits.
